From f51fb77d78bce4a3549c021c4a68119d28f260af Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: dardiao <xn--6s1a@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 19 Sep 2026 23:00:53 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 09/14] local: replace the bundled lemmy icon with the site's
 own mark
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

The favicon, the apple-touch icon and the PWA icons all shipped the upstream Lemmy logo, and
since the site had no icon configured they were what every visitor saw in their browser tab.

The new mark is a geometric 「牛」 (four strokes, no font dependency) on a dark badge: the
rounded badge is for favicon.svg, the full-bleed square is for the home-screen/PWA PNGs, which
is how those platforms expect their icons.
